bianbu-agent-runtime (0.1.163) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Stop declaring security state in the Agent editor. The starter Agent no
    longer ships a `permissions` block or `metadata.execution.requested_mode`,
    and the Expert editor drops the capability policy table, the JSON policy
    panel, the network scope, the personal-data policy and the host/sandbox
    selector. A new Expert is simply host + yolo until an operator configures
    it in the security console. `metadata.runtime.requested_mode` and
    `metadata.execution.requested_mode` are rejected as retired.
  * Derive the Worker execution boundary from the Agent's security settings.
    `_requested_execution_mode` always returns `auto` and the supervisor asks
    securityd; a Worker only runs sandboxed once a read, write, network or
    syscall setting is declared. A new Expert therefore starts on the host.
  * Register only missing tool policies. `ensure_capabilities` reads the
    existing rows and registers what securityd has not seen, so restarting the
    Runtime never rolls back an operator's tightening. The DLP policy sync is
    gone with it; DLP rows belong to the security console.
  * Move the security permission settings onto their own console page. The
    read and write scopes are include + exclude pairs and the execution mode is
    shown read-only as the derived result. The syscall blacklist page states
    that nothing is restricted by default.
  * `RUNTIME_MANIFEST_VERSION` advances because the packaged Agent package
    changed and securityd rejects a manifest rollback.

