    is a network deadline, and applied to 127.0.0.1 it measures the device's
    own prompt prefill: on K3 a local Qwen3VL-4B server spent 109 s encoding a
    64x64 image and the image reading tool failed with provider_timeout after
    120 s, discarding an answer the model had already produced. A Provider
    record may now set `request_timeout_seconds` explicitly, a loopback Base
    URL defaults to fifteen minutes, and a network endpoint keeps two minutes.

