    servers. The verb only wrote mcp.json before, so the first Run paid for
    the npm download inside the 30s budget shared with tool calls and a cold
    npx start on K3 (23.2s) could leave the generation without those tools
    while every surface still reported success. Such declarations are now
    installed once into `<data_dir>/mcp-runtime/<id>` through a staging
    directory renamed into place and started as `node <script>`, and every
    stdio declaration is started once and asked for its tools before the
    configuration is written: a server that cannot start exits 1 with the
    reason and installs nothing. `--no-verify` skips that check and
    `--upgrade` replaces an installed name; `remove` drops the vendored tree
    together with the declaration. `timeout_seconds` (30s) is now only the
    per-call budget, and the new `startup_timeout_seconds` is what starting a
    server waits with. The result and the API resource gained the server's
    real state (`status`, `tools`, `detail`, `vendored`,
    `startup_timeout_seconds`) so a failed install is visible instead of
    reported as success.

 -- liudecheng[bot] <decheng.liu@spacemit.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800

bianbu-agent-runtime (0.1.129) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

