bianbu-agent-runtime (0.1.128) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Resolve the Runtime run identity once and keep it stable, and support
    installing as root. An install performed as root directly over SSH has no
    SUDO_USER and no non-root logname, so it could only fall back to uid 1000;
    when that uid belongs to another account the device recorded the wrong
    identity. It now falls back further to the lowest regular account (uid
    1000..65533). A previously recorded identity now also wins over logname and
    the uid fallback, because the identity belongs to the device rather than to
    whoever ran apt, so a reinstall or upgrade always lands on the same
    ~/.bianbu-agent. A record whose account was deleted is no longer reused -
    that left the drop-in pointing at a non-existent user - and is re-resolved
    instead.

