bianbu-agent-runtime (0.1.124) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Show security-center timestamps in the local time zone. securityd sends
    ISO-8601 UTC, but the console printed the string as-is, so the wall clock
    was one time zone ahead of the page (8 hours on CST boards); the same
    column also fell back to the raw SQLite UTC form for Agents that only had
    an installation time. The "recent activity" column now parses the value
    (naive timestamps are UTC and get a Z), shows "just now" / "N minutes ago"
    for the last hour and the local clock afterwards, prints "no activity yet"
    instead of an installation timestamp, and keeps the installation time in
    the tooltip. The syscall-audit and audit-log time columns use the same
    local formatting.

