bianbu-agent-runtime (0.1.55) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Skip an unloadable system Agent declaration instead of failing startup.
    A profile directory outlives the Runtime that published it and the Runtime
    cannot rewrite a root-owned profile in place, so a record written by a
    retired generation (an Agent that still declared `hooks`, for example)
    stopped the process from starting with "unsupported agent fields".  The
    record is now named in the log and treated as absent, exactly like an
    unloadable user record, so a source checkout can start against its own
    leftover profile.

