 -- liudecheng <decheng.liu@spacemit.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:40:00 +0800

bianbu-agent-runtime (0.1.45) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Remove the compatibility layer for retired first-party formats.  The
    Runtime no longer migrates data written by earlier generations: the
    `session-logs/` transcript root, the per-Agent JSON records (and their
    `cache/agent-json-migration` backup), the standalone MCP package that used
    to live directly under `plugins/`, and the legacy project-provider claim in
    the Model store are gone.  A file or record in one of those formats is now
    left untouched instead of being rewritten, so an upgrade cannot silently
    reinterpret user data.
  * Tighten the Agent and Plugin contracts that those formats depended on.
    `plugin.yaml` and `agent.yaml` reject the retired keys (`agent.hooks`,
    `agent.model` as a bare string, legacy `plugins` absence), an Agent
    selection is never `None`, and the API no longer reports the
    `legacy_plugin_selection` projection field.  Hooks, Tools and Skills are
    selected only through the Plugin that owns them.
  * Remove the package-oriented `bianbu-agent mcp install/show/verify`
    subcommands, the MCP legacy-plugin migration, the `PluginManager.snapshot`
    alias, the `CompressionSettingsProvider` settings-file argument and the
    retired standalone Intent MCP that package provisioning used to preserve.
    An Agent that declares no model still uses the model the SDK injected as
    its default, while a hand-written Provider record in the retired
    project-provider shape is no longer adopted: only a read-only packaged
    record may be shadowed by the project pair.

 -- liudecheng <decheng.liu@spacemit.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:10:00 +0800

bianbu-agent-runtime (0.1.44) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Ignore a capability Inventory file that carries no managed schema.  A
    stale zero-byte `inventory.sqlite3` (or one left by a retired writer) made
    every capability read fail with `invalid capability Inventory`, so
    `/api/v1/agents` answered 422 and the Console reported the Runtime as
    unavailable on K3.  Missing, empty and schema-less files now read as an
    empty Inventory; a file that holds the schema but cannot be read still
    fails, and the Runtime logs the file it ignored.

 -- liudecheng <decheng.liu@spacemit.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:05:00 +0800

bianbu-agent-runtime (0.1.43) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Redefine the Plugin package contract.  `plugin.yaml` now carries identity
    only: `schema_version`, `name`, `version` and the optional `description`,
    `dependencies`, `config_schema` and `entrypoint`.  What a package provides
    is the package itself, so `tools/`, `skills/`, `hooks/`, `mcps/` and an
    optional `console.py` are scanned instead of declared.  The `id` key is
    renamed to `name`, and `sdk_version`, `permissions` and `contributions` are
    removed; unknown keys are rejected rather than interpreted, so there is
    nothing left to keep in sync between a manifest and a directory.  Host
    compatibility is now the `schema_version` the Runtime implements, which
    removes the second version range and the approval gate.
  * Drop the `apc-plugin.json` fallback and the marketplace package reader.
    Another agent's manifest is no longer used for identity or for a Skill
    closure, and a package that still ships one is rejected as an unsupported
    entry, so every publisher ships this contract's own `plugin.yaml`.
  * Remove the Plugin permission model.  Installing a Plugin is the trust
    decision, so a package's Hooks may deny or transform a Run without an
    approved-permission set.  `PluginPermission`, `HookContribution.permissions`
    and the permission fields of the Plugin API views are gone.
  * Report Plugin member IDs qualified by their owner in `plugin members`, and
    point a qualified ID handed to `skill show`, `skill verify`, `skill remove`
    or `mcp show`/`verify` at that command instead of failing a bare
    directory-name check.
  * Keep bundled Audit, Bibit Intent, Memory and Security Plugins on the new
    contract, and align the plugin-creator Skill, the CLI guide and the
    extension guides with it.

